  "term": "categorical data analysis",
  "definition": "Categorical data analysis is the statistical analysis of data sorted into classes or outcomes rather than measured on a continuous scale. It is used for variables such as nominal, ordinal, or two-choice outcomes and applies methods suited to frequencies or proportions, especially when studying binary or multinomial results.",
